WEBVTT

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:16.000
Ionodai, aiming to become the
skate-leading national champions,

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.500
face the Grand Prix Series along with me,
the brilliantly talented Hayato Sasugai.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:26.290
It all hinges on how we utilize
Kensei Maeshima, the forgotten genius,

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.750
who experiences extreme ups and downs.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:33.450
With some unease remaining,
the day came upon us.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:35.500
Hey, we're gonna be fine, right?

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:36.620
"13th Men’s High School Skate-Leading Grand Prix
Opening Ceremonies, First Competition Venue"

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:40.620
"13th Men’s High School Skate-Leading Grand Prix
Opening Ceremonies, First Competition Venue"

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:40.620
At long last, the season opens for the year.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:44.120
"13th Men’s High School Skate-Leading Grand Prix
Opening Ceremonies, First Competition Venue"

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:44.120
The Men's High School Skate-Leading Grand Prix--

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:48.450
Which team will shine as Japan's
number one this year?

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:53.870
All 16 schools have gathered here
at Makinohara Ice Arena.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:56.500
"St. Clavis" "Nagano Koryo" "Otaru"

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:56.500
We will now have last year's champion,

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.830
"St. Clavis" "Nagano Koryo" "Otaru"

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.830
St. Clavis Gakuin High School of
Tokyo Prefecture, return the championship flag.

00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:01.750
St. Clavis Gakuin High School of
Tokyo Prefecture, return the championship flag.

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:15.000
Taiga Himuro, third year at St. Clavis
High School, will also recite the oath.

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:19.330
In the name of all the athletes,

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:21.830
we promise to honor the spirit of skate-leading.

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:24.750
For the many people involved
who have assisted us,

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:28.790
and the judges, referees, and our supporters,

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:34.500
we promise to skate fairly and honorably.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.750
I hope that this competition will further
the understanding of skate-leading,

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:43.200
increase the number of athletes,
and raise its popularity,

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.160
which in turn will lead
to the future of this sport.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:50.910
Formalities aside, this is two months long,
so we're in it for the long haul.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:54.540
Take care of your bodies
while having some fun, guys!

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:56.290
That's just like him.

00:01:56.290 --> 00:02:00.870
Third year, captain of
St. Clavis Gakuin, Taiga Himuro.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.450
"Episode 6
Indecision"

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:49.290
I'll review the rules for the Men's High School
Skate-Leading Grand Prix Series.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:52.700
The competing schools consist
of the six seeded schools

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:55.120
from last year's Grand Prix Series finals,

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:56.450
plus the 10 schools with the highest scores
at last month's preliminaries

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:58.450
"Seeded Schools"

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:58.450
plus the 10 schools with the highest scores
at last month's preliminaries

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:00.080
"Seeded Schools"

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:00.080
for a total of 16 schools.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.250
"Seeded Schools"  "Schools From Preliminaries"

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.250
for a total of 16 schools.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:05.750
"Grand Prix Series Participate
in 3 of 8 competitions"

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:05.750
Each school will compete in three
lottery-assigned competitions

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:07.910
"Grand Prix Series Participate
in 3 of 8 competitions"

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:07.910
that take place around the country.

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:12.370
After the eighth competition,
the six top-scoring schools

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:14.500
move on to the Grand Prix finals
and are seeded in next year's competition.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:17.000
"Compete in Grand Prix Finals
+ Seeded Next Year"

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:17.000
move on to the Grand Prix finals
and are seeded in next year's competition.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.830
Here's Ms. Abe, our commentator.

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:22.790
As always, since the first competition
directly follows the opening ceremonies,

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:26.700
you see many of our athletes in the stands.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:30.040
Which teams do you have
your eye on this year, Ms. Abe?

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.950
First, I must say last
year's champion, St. Clavis.

00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:38.250
Including their captain, Himuro, they have
three starting members from last year.

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:40.120
With the addition of Shinozaki,

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:43.540
you can indisputably say that
they're the strongest team here.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:44.540
Any others?

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:47.040
I'm also watching out for last year's
runner up, Nagano Koryo High School

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:51.500
and Otaru Technical High School,
who placed third.

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.120
"Aichi Prefecture Chutei University Kamimaezu High School
Waiting Room"

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.120
But there's last year's sixth,
Chutei University Kamimaezu High School.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.910
"Aichi Prefecture Chutei University Kamimaezu High School
Waiting Room"

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.910
With their twin aces,
the elder, Hajime Ishikawa,

00:04:56.910 --> 00:05:01.700
and the younger, Susumu Ishikawa,
they seem to have honed the unison skating

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:05.290
that they're known for.

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:08.580
What about Ionodai High School,
who placed fourth last year?

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:12.620
Their coach is now the skater Adachi,
who is recovering from an injury.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:17.500
I'm familiar with Adachi's skill as a skater,
but not so much as a coach yet.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:20.750
Do you think the return of Shinozaki's
rival from his novice days,

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:24.750
Kensei Maeshima, will give them an edge?

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:27.040
It depends on how much
he's compensated for his break.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:29.790
Their ace, Himekawa, also transferred
to Kogahara High School

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:33.080
right before this series.

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:36.290
Kogahara High School came
at the top of the preliminaries.

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:38.500
They will be skating at today's competition.

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:43.910
Himekawa is part of the cream of the crop team
that the famed Coach Kumada leads.

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.450
Formidable, indeed.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:50.450
But I must say, the hottest school
from the preliminaries

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.830
has to be Yokohama Super Global High School.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:57.500
Though their abilities as a team are
yet unknown, Kuonji, who skated overseas,

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.910
is leading them forward as their captain.

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:02.450
I look forward to watching a routine
filled with high school energy.

00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:06.200
"13th Men's High School
Skate-Leading Grand Prix"

00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:06.200
This year's Grand Prix Series
is truly a rivalry of warlords.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:09.160
"13th Men's High School
Skate-Leading Grand Prix"

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:09.160
The first competition we've all
been waiting for will begin soon!

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.370
Whoa, whoa, whoa...

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:14.040
What are you doing?

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.660
It's time for our meeting.

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:17.040
Hurry up and get back to the waiting room.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:18.910
Shouldn't I buy this? It's only sold
here and it's commemorative!

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:21.660
"New Item"

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:21.660
Shouldn't I buy this? It's only sold
here and it's commemorative!

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:24.790
Commemorative of what? Don't get carried away.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:25.910
Come on.

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.540
Listen up, everyone.

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:38.080
We're last of the six teams
to skate for the short program.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:41.040
"1. Tanabe Ryujin 2. Ajigasawa Meisei
3. Gunma Jomo Academy 4. Kurume Chuo"

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:41.040
Make sure to do a thorough warmup
to keep your bodies warm.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:44.160
We know. We always do.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:45.370
Stop that.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:48.080
The most powerful team in this first competition

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:50.790
"Chutei University Kamimaezu"

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:50.790
has to be Chutei University High.

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:53.370
They're very synchronized, have a solid routine,

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:57.000
and have expanded the breadth
of their presentation this year.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.620
But if we skate like we did
at training camp, we can win.

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:01.660
--Let's do this!
--Yeah!

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:02.660
Coach?

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:08.790
Yeah, Terauchi's said everything
I would've said. You guys aren't bad.

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:09.910
Yes, sir!

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:14.160
I'm counting on you to skate
as we practiced, Maeshima.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:16.200
Leave it to me.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:16.950
Tch.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:19.700
What? Did you have something to say?

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:21.250
No.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:24.410
Tomo, let's go to the practice rink.
Scouting out the enemy.

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:25.370
O-Okay.

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:26.540
"Skating Rink Directory" "1F Main Rink"

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:30.250
"Skating Rink Directory" "1F Main Rink"

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:30.250
The first three teams are
using the lower practice rink.

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:31.500
"Skating Rink Directory" "1F Main Rink"

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:31.500
The three teams skating
in the second half go later.

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:32.500
"1F Main Rink" "B1F Practice Rink"

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:32.500
The three teams skating
in the second half go later.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:34.500
"1F Main Rink" "B1F Practice Rink"

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:34.500
Come one at a time for me to do your makeup.

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:36.450
"1F Main Rink" "B1F Practice Rink"

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:36.450
Tell me if there's something up
with your outfit.

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:37.580
"1F Main Rink" "B1F Practice Rink"

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:37.580
I'll fix it right up.

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:38.620
"1F Main Rink" "B1F Practice Rink"

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:38.620
Yessir!

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:40.830
Mm...

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:43.660
Sh-Shinozaki?

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:45.290
--Credit card.
--You want those?!

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:53.410
They're all good.
That's the Grand Prix Series for you.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:56.040
Guess so. We'll go by skating order.

00:07:56.040 --> 00:08:01.660
First, Tanabe Ryujin High School. 42.94, 44.39.

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:02.950
--Huh?
--Write it down.

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:04.290
O-Oh, right.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:09.080
Second, Ajigasawa Meisei. 43.10, 45.14.

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:15.370
Third, Gunma Jomo Academy. 37.97, 41.61.

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:20.370
This now concludes the six-minute warmup.
The competition will begin shortly.

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:22.370
That's about it.

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:24.370
Sasugai, is this--

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:26.120
Come on. We'll check these upstairs.

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:28.620
The competition will begin shortly.

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:34.120
Skaters in the second half of the
short program, head to the practice rink.

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:37.250
Your six-minute warmup will begin shortly.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.330
All right!

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:40.790
Hey, you're not done yet!

00:08:53.830 --> 00:08:55.870
Do you and Shinozaki know each other?

00:08:55.870 --> 00:08:58.660
Yeah, something like that.

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:01.580
Hey, where were you, Shinozaki?

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:02.410
What's up?

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:03.950
It's nothing.

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:06.620
The six-minute warmup
for second-half skaters is starting.

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:09.080
Let's go cheer Terauchi and the others on.

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:18.750
Hm? Aren't those your former teammates, Izumi?

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:22.750
I remember the kid with the glasses.
Go ahead and talk to them.

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:25.160
No, there's no need.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:28.040
You're so cold.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:30.500
Actually, just the opposite, huh?

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:36.200
Why, it's been so long, Soejima!

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:38.370
Here comes the pain in the neck.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:43.370
--Kakeru! Banri! Iori! Rui!

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:45.620
--Stop! Please stop!
--Kakeru! Banri! Iori! Rui!

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:46.580
Soejima?

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:47.540
It's “Maeshima.”

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:48.500
You don't have to correct him.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:49.790
Oh! I need an autograph board!

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:55.080
I did invite you to join my team before.
I came to wish you luck.

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:56.620
Even though you've got his name wrong?

00:09:56.620 --> 00:10:00.200
I'll be waiting at the Grand Prix finals.

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:02.660
You assume you'll get there already?

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:08.160
Is he tense since he's competing today?

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:09.580
Hey.

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:11.700
I'm writing on the first competition.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:16.120
I'll be paying close attention to your coaching.

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:18.790
First to skate, Tanabe Ryujin High School.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:29.830
"Tanabe Ryujin High School"

00:10:31.910 --> 00:10:34.330
"Ajigasawa Meisei High School"

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:38.950
"Gunma Jomo Academy High School"

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:40.950
"1. Tanabe Ryujin"   "Sasugai’s prediction"    "Result"

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:51.200
That concludes the first half
of the short program.

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:53.040
The second half will commence

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:57.370
following a 15-minute intermission
to resurface the ice.

00:10:57.370 --> 00:11:02.750
This now concludes the six-minute warmup.
Teams practicing, please clear the ice.

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:05.160
The competition will resume shortly.

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:10.120
Hey.

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:11.000
Himuro.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:14.040
We'll compete again at the Grand Prix finals.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:15.870
Don't trip up here.

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:19.120
Right back at you.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:22.830
Himuro.

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:26.540
Keep your cool. You can
be scatterbrained at times.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:28.790
That's not true!

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.330
Just you watch, Shinozaki.

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:50.200
39.42, 42.07.

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:51.120
Hm?

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:52.500
--Write it down.
--O-Oh.

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:55.080
"Kurume Chuo High School"

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:55.080
A total of 81.26.

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:57.950
"Kurume Chuo High School"

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:57.950
Fourth to skate, Kurume Chuo High School
scores short of expectations,

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:02.540
putting them in third place
for the short program.

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:05.790
Their failure to recover from
an early mistake hurt them.

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:09.410
"3. Kurume Chuo High School"

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:09.410
Did it upset them? Their teamwork
seemed a little disrupted.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:13.620
Coming up to skate fifth is last year's
sixth and one of the favorites to win,

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:17.330
Chutei University Kamimaezu High School.

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:19.870
What kind of performance will they give us?

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:50.250
Great unison from the start,
a specialty of the Ishikawa brothers!

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:52.750
They're taking great advantage
of their double leads.

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.830
The wing and guards are also performing calmly.

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:58.790
If they keep this up, we can expect high scores.

00:12:58.790 --> 00:12:59.750
They're good.

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:03.750
Yes, their synchronization is stunning.

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:07.580
I see how they've honed
their skill since last year.

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:23.660
They're amazing.

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:26.620
Yeah, but it's no surprise.

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:32.160
45.58, 44.66. Total, 90.24.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:33.200
Huh?

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:34.200
What?

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:47.580
They landed the jump! Chutei University High
has delivered a perfect program!

00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:50.080
This should place them pretty high.

00:14:00.790 --> 00:14:02.330
They've won this.

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:06.830
Yes, they definitely got first.
Just need to see their point lead.

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:09.250
Well, well, very impressive.

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:13.540
This is an example of the opponents
you'll face at the Grand Prix finals.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:15.660
True, their technique was exceptional.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:20.870
But skating in unison isn't the
deciding factor in skate-leading.

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:25.410
Skate-leading is fascinating.

00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:26.330
Right?

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:29.540
"Chutei University Kamimaezu High School"

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:29.540
Now, for the scores we've been waiting for...

00:14:29.540 --> 00:14:31.370
"Chutei University Kamimaezu High School"

00:14:29.540 --> 00:14:31.370
A total of 90.36.
They've blasted their way to the top!

00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:33.370
"1. Chutei University Kamimaezu High School"

00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:33.370
They've blasted their way to the top!

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:35.250
It's higher than I thought.

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:37.500
Hah, we've just got to win.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:39.750
Shinozaki's in the audience watching.

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:43.450
I know. I saw him earlier downstairs.

00:14:43.450 --> 00:14:44.450
What?

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:47.120
Don't worry. I'm calm--

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:49.200
--That's not the issue.
Are you really here to win--

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:53.000
--Next, skating in sixth,
Ionodai High School, Saitama Prefecture.
--That's not the issue.
Are you really here to win--

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:53.870
Let's go!

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:55.080
Yeah!

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:03.750
Tch.

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:05.870
Next up is Ionodai that placed fourth last year.

00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:08.540
Let's see what kind of performance
they'll give this year.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:39.750
Ionodai High School is also using a two lead,
one wing, two guard formation.

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:42.910
How will they use this strategy to score points?

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:46.620
They're doing great.
All five are in sync from the start.

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:02.450
They landed a jump combination!

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:04.250
Great jumps with great synchronization!

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:05.370
Oh?

00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:09.660
Compared to last year, the individual athletes
have improved in technique and stability.

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:12.950
Is this the result of
Coach Adachi's instruction?

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:16.580
Spectacular. Very tidy teamwork.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:24.040
Maeshima had a four-year break,
but it doesn't show in his great performance!

00:16:38.500 --> 00:16:42.250
Ionodai has completed the program
without any major mistakes!

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:48.450
Hey, you see that?

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:55.080
Now, what are the results?

00:16:56.290 --> 00:16:57.580
"Ionodai High School"

00:16:57.580 --> 00:17:01.290
"Ionodai High School"

00:16:57.580 --> 00:17:01.290
A total of 89.54! Not enough to take
the top from Chutei University High,

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:02.620
"2. Ionodai High School"

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:02.620
A total of 89.54! Not enough to take
the top from Chutei University High,

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:04.620
"2. Ionodai High School"

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:04.620
but coming in a close second!

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:07.500
--All right!
--Damn, not good enough, huh?

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:09.200
No, we did good.

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:13.250
We already knew that Chutei High
had the advantage for the short program.

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:15.000
We just need to turn it around
in the free skate.

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:15.830
--Okay.
--Yeah.

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:17.000
'Course we will.

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:21.580
Hm, so this is how they
pulled the team together?

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:24.450
What the hell was that?

00:17:24.450 --> 00:17:26.950
Wait, Shinozaki. I know how you feel...

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:29.080
Wh-What? What's wrong?

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:30.750
I've lost interest.

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:31.620
Huh?

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:33.950
I know the results. At this rate...

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:34.120
"Saitama Prefecture Ionodai High School
Waiting Room"

00:17:34.120 --> 00:17:36.830
"Saitama Prefecture Ionodai High School
Waiting Room"

00:17:34.120 --> 00:17:36.830
We're going to lose to Chutei High
in the free skate, too.

00:17:36.830 --> 00:17:38.500
--What do you mean?!
--Icchan!

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:39.950
Exactly what I said.

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:41.160
On what grounds?

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:42.410
My predictions.

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:43.830
Big deal.

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:47.700
B-But, Sasugai's score predictions
for the other teams were mostly correct

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:49.540
after just watching their warmup.

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:51.080
Take a look at this.

00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:55.000
The first number is his how he scored
the warmup. The bottom, their actual score.

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:57.160
Wow, they're mostly on.

00:17:57.160 --> 00:18:00.700
He predicted Chutei High's score
before they even finished.

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:04.290
So you're saying that we'll lose at this rate?

00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:06.080
What are you telling us to do, then?

00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:09.620
Changing our free skate routine
now is way too risky.

00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:11.660
I didn't say anything about changing it.

00:18:11.660 --> 00:18:14.910
You should let Maeshima skate more freely.

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:20.830
He was great when he was wild.
They've tamed him, huh?

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:25.910
Maeshima, why are you being
such a goody two shoes?

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:28.830
Fine, match the others.
This is a team sport, after all.

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:31.450
But don't conform too much.

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:35.580
I'm looking forward to your
explosive power. That's the key.

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:37.870
There are plenty of athletes with just skill.

00:18:37.870 --> 00:18:41.200
Won't he revert back to how
he was before the training camp?

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.290
Zooming around and stuff.

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:44.250
He might.

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:45.830
What?!

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:50.370
What's this team's goal?
Isn't it to become the national champions?

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:54.950
Or are you satisfied to qualify
for the finals? Yay, whoopee?

00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:57.290
The other teams are competing fiercely.

00:18:57.290 --> 00:18:59.620
A team suddenly grows stronger
and snatches a great score.

00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:03.250
Isn't that what high school
sports are all about?!

00:19:03.250 --> 00:19:06.040
Isn't that what they said about you
when you placed fourth at nationals

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:07.790
in your second year?

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:09.500
Don't go on the defensive!

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:11.330
When did you become the ones being challenged?

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:12.950
After placing a mere fourth at nationals?

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:15.160
That's not right. You're the ones
coming from behind, right?

00:19:15.160 --> 00:19:16.700
Aren't you the challengers?

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:19.250
But to drop out in the first competition...

00:19:19.250 --> 00:19:22.330
It's just the opposite! It's <i>because</i>
this is the first competition.

00:19:22.330 --> 00:19:26.120
What if in the third competition,
the top school's got a huge lead on you?

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:28.330
Will you make a reckless attempt
in the third competition?

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:32.580
Or would you rather try it now and
give yourselves time to modify it?

00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:36.450
Between qualifying for the finals
at the top and barely scraping by in sixth,

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:39.500
which do you think will give you
better momentum? Which one, huh?!

00:19:41.250 --> 00:19:43.160
Don't cower.

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:46.120
Or was your declaration to become
national champions all for show?

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:54.370
Ah, to be young. You idiots.

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:55.200
Coach...

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:58.540
What Sasugai said hits the mark.

00:19:58.540 --> 00:20:01.950
At this rate, it'll be tough to be on top.

00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:07.160
Earning safe points is one strategy. But...

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:10.700
Maeshima. What do you want to do?

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:13.450
I-I...

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:21.750
I want to win.

00:20:21.750 --> 00:20:23.660
Kiriyama...

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:31.410
Maeshima, give it a shot.

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:32.660
Are you serious?

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:37.910
We want to win! We want
to become national champions!

00:20:37.910 --> 00:20:40.500
If there's a way to achieve
that right in front of us...

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:46.000
I don't believe that we're a team
that would crumble if it does fail.

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:47.080
Maeshima!

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:51.330
"Ionodai

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:54.700
"Ionodai
Free Skate"

00:20:57.250 --> 00:20:59.870
We're almost up.

00:20:59.870 --> 00:21:02.580
Chutei University High shakes off
the teams snapping at its heels

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:04.790
to take a solid first!

00:21:04.790 --> 00:21:07.080
Looks like they received high
performance and technical points

00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:09.450
from elements in the middle of their routine.

00:21:09.450 --> 00:21:10.500
That was good.

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:12.830
Yeah.

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:14.330
Are you actually nervous?

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:17.500
O-Of course. Who wouldn't be?

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:19.830
Don't worry, Maeshima.

00:21:19.830 --> 00:21:22.660
We're the ones who decided
to do this. Skate freely.

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:24.500
We'll back you up.

00:21:27.540 --> 00:21:28.330
Our next routine is by Ionodai High School,

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:29.080
"Ionodai High School" "Lead: Kensei Maeshima
Guard: Shotaro Terauchi Lead: Itsuki Kiriyama
Wing: Akimitsu Mochizuki Guard: Sota Jonouchi"

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:29.080
Our next routine is by Ionodai High School,

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:32.660
"Ionodai High School" "Lead: Kensei Maeshima
Guard: Shotaro Terauchi Lead: Itsuki Kiriyama
Wing: Akimitsu Mochizuki Guard: Sota Jonouchi"

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:32.660
who stood in second after the short program.

00:21:32.660 --> 00:21:36.120
They seemed somewhat rigid
during the short program,

00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:37.700
but how will they do in the free skate?

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:53.750
For the first competition
of the Grand Prix Series,

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:54.700
our team ended up in sixth place.

00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:58.160
"6. Ionodai High School"

00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:58.160
our team ended up in sixth place.

00:21:59.410 --> 00:22:03.370
What a way to lose. But...

00:22:03.370 --> 00:22:04.500
...it wasn't bad.

00:23:35.910 --> 00:23:36.830
"Next time" "Resolution"

00:23:36.830 --> 00:23:39.080
"Next time" "Resolution"

00:23:36.830 --> 00:23:39.080
I've had no problems conversing
after coming to Niigata.

00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:41.910
"Next time" "Resolution"

00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:41.910
Is there no more dialect?

00:23:41.910 --> 00:23:45.330
"Next time" "Resolution"

00:23:41.910 --> 00:23:45.330
Say no more. There are certain
<i>circumstances</i> for the writers.

00:23:45.330 --> 00:23:49.080
"Next time" "Resolution"

00:23:45.330 --> 00:23:49.080
--Circumstances?
--By the way, I'm actually
speaking in Russian right now.

00:23:49.080 --> 00:23:49.910
"Next time" "Resolution"

00:23:49.080 --> 00:23:49.910
You're joking!

00:23:49.910 --> 00:23:50.870
"Next time" "Resolution"

00:23:49.910 --> 00:23:50.870
Yeah, I'm joking.
